oido-dictate (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New engine oido-hybrid (GPU add-on, Pi 4/400): a long phrase (>= 4.5 s) with a real
    pause is cut there; the GPU transcribes the head while the CPU (cores 1-3, nice 19)
    transcribes the tail. Any CPU problem falls back to the whole phrase on the GPU.
    Default engine is still oido-gpu-lm.
  * Pi 5 (and other dotprod CPUs): the CPU engine binary tasr_cli_dotprod_static is rebuilt with
    4x4 sdot GEMM, 4-row sdot attention and NEON softmax/activation/im2col/dequant. Logits are
    bit-identical to the old build; ~1.5x faster on 3 Cortex-A720 cores (Pixel 9 VM stand-in),
    NOT yet measured on a real Pi 5.

 -- Tarel <334372633+tarelerulz@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000

oido-dictate (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: 0.1.1 changed encoder outputs slightly (not bit-exact), which could change
    LM-beam text on some clips. Logits are bit-identical to 0.1.0 again.
  * Still faster than 0.1.0 on the CPU engine (4x4 NEON GEMM, H*T attention split).

 -- Tarel <334372633+tarelerulz@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0000

oido-dictate (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * CPU engine ~1.8x faster (4x4 NEON int8 GEMM, H*T attention split, cached
    position projections); transcripts identical. Rebuilt static a72 and dotprod tasr_cli.
  * GPU kit: faster readback, C greedy argmax, plan cache (3-7% faster).
  * Pi 5 dotprod binary rebuilt from the same source (compile-checked, not run on a Pi 5).

 -- Tarel <334372633+tarelerulz@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:10:00 +0000

oido-dictate (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging.
  * oido-dictate: CPU engine (static tasr_cli + LM) + Speak window + punctuation.
  * oido-dictate-gpu: V3D 4.2 GPU engine add-on (Pi 4 / 400 / CM4).
  * Model weights downloaded on first run, not bundled.

